# aether-keyword-statement-mappings

Complete authoritative mapping of Aether keywords to their conventional equivalents: conduit=def, flow=return, fork/path=if/elif/else, swirl=while/for, contain/spill/finally=try/except/finally, dam=break, divert=continue, trickle=yield, fracture=raise, still=pass, evaporate=del, siphon=import, verify=assert, mold=class, use=with, inspect/match=match/case, ocean=global, outer=nonlocal.

## Procedures
- 1. Function definition: `conduit Name(~params) { suite }`.
- 2. Return: `flow [expression]`.
- 3. If/elif/else: `fork (cond) -> { } path (cond) -> { } path -> { }`.
- 4. While loop: `swirl (expression) { suite }`.
- 5. For-each loop: `swirl (~item in ~iterable) { suite }`.
- 6. Try/except/finally: `contain { } spill (~err) { } finally { }`.
- 7. Break: `dam`.
- 8. Continue: `divert`.
- 9. Yield: `trickle expression`.
- 10. Raise: `fracture [expression]`.
- 11. Pass (no-op): `still`.
- 12. Del: `evaporate target_list`.
- 13. Import: `siphon module [as alias]` or `siphon name from module`.
- 14. Assert: `verify expression [, message]` — raises `AssertionFracture` on failure.
- 15. Class definition: `mold Name extends Base { suite }`.
- 16. With/context manager: `use (~resource) { suite }`.
- 17. Structural pattern match: `inspect (~val) { match pattern -> { } }`.
- 18. Global declaration: `ocean name`.
- 19. Nonlocal declaration: `outer name`.
- 20. Lambda: `conduit(~x) -> { flow ~x + 1 }`.
- 21. Async coroutine: `tributary` modifier on conduit; await: `~result << merge ~handle`.

## Conventions
- All compound statement conditions are wrapped in parentheses: `fork (cond) ->`, `swirl (cond) {`.
- Compound statement bodies use `->` arrow before a brace block for fork/path/inspect/match.
- `swirl` unifies while and for-in — the in-keyword variant is the for-each form.
- Exception variable in spill is a Wave identifier: `spill (~err)`.

